MCP:model context protocol

Earlier, every LLM application connected to tools using custom code and different architectures. There was no standardized or universal protocol for how LLMs should discover, access, and use tools. MCP (Model Context Protocol) was introduced to provide a standardized way for LLMs to connect with tools, APIs, memory, databases, and external systems to build interoperable AI agents.

You can think of MCP like:

USB-C for AI agents

Before MCP:

every framework had different integrations
tools were tightly coupled
difficult interoperability
difficult portability between models/frameworks

With MCP:

standard tool interface
standard context sharing
reusable agent ecosystems
easier multi-agent/tool orchestration

Architecture idea:

LLM ↔ MCP Protocol ↔ Tools/Memory/APIs

Examples of tools:

web search
databases
filesystem
GitHub
Slack
calendar
code execution

So MCP is essentially:

a protocol layer
for standardized AI-agent communication with tools and context systems

Very similar to how:

HTTP standardized web communication
USB standardized hardware connection
MCP standardizes AI tool connectivity